<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy — Apple requires this file to accept an App Store submission.

  READ THIS BEFORE YOU SHIP A FORK OF THIS TEMPLATE.

  What is declared below is the truth for the TEMPLATE AS SHIPPED, which does nothing but render
  three Compose screens and an AI panel that has no key configured. It stores nothing, tracks
  nothing, and calls none of Apple's "required reason" APIs. That is a deliberately empty starting
  point, not a default you can leave alone: the moment your app saves a preference, reads a file,
  or adds an analytics SDK, this file is out of date and has to be edited.

  Over-declaring is a false statement to Apple. Under-declaring gets the submission rejected.
  Declare what your code actually does, and grep for it rather than guessing.

  The four required-reason categories most likely to apply to an app grown from this template,
  with the reason code for the ordinary case. Uncomment the matching block in
  NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes when the usage becomes real:

    NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults   CA92.1  reading/writing your OWN app's defaults.
                                                       Needed as soon as anything reaches
                                                       NSUserDefaults — for example swapping
                                                       kmp-toolkit's KeychainSettings for
                                                       NSUserDefaultsSettings, or adding
                                                       multiplatform-settings with its default
                                                       iOS backend. NOT needed today: this
                                                       template's only secure storage path is
                                                       :llm-chat's SecureKeyStore, which uses the
                                                       Keychain, and the Keychain is not a
                                                       required-reason API.
    NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp  C617.1  reading a file's creation/modification date.
    NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime 35F9.1  measuring elapsed time from boot time.
    NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace      E174.1  checking available disk space.

  NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes describes data that LEAVES the device. The template sends nothing:
  its AI panel ships with no provider key, so no prompt ever reaches a server. Wire a real key
  through :llm-chat and prompts become collected data you must declare here.

  Reference: https://developer.apple.com/documentation/bundleresources/privacy_manifest_files
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- The template neither tracks users nor links data to third-party data for advertising. -->
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>

	<!-- Must stay empty while NSPrivacyTracking is false; Apple rejects the combination otherwise. -->
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>

	<!-- Nothing leaves the device. See the note on the AI panel above. -->
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>

	<!-- No required-reason API is reached by the template's own code. See the table above. -->
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
